 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to increasing the sales and\ncompensating use taxes for the county of Steuben",
    "basePrintNo": "S8345",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8345-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1262-h, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8345\n\nSPONSOR: O'MARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to increasing the sales and\ncompensating use taxes for the county of Steuben\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo make technical changes to Budget Bill A.9504-B, chapter 58 of the\nLaws of 2020 to authorize the Steuben County Legislature to increase the\nsales tax distribution amounts to the various municipalities, towns and\nvillages.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThe bill amends section 1262-h of the tax law to authorize Steuben Coun-\nty to extend an additional one percent sales tax ending November 30,\n2023.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Steuben County Legislature had passed a resolution requesting that\nthe New York State Legislature introduce and pass a bill to authorize\nthe county to extend their existing additional 1% sales and use tax.\nThis bill is to correct a technical amendment that is a result of Budget\nBill A.9508-8, Chapter 58 of the laws of 2020 authorizing and extending\nSteuben County's sales tax but not updating the distribution amounts as\nset forth in A.9704-A. Steuben County expressly delineates the amount of\ntaxes distributed to the City of Hornell, the City of Corning and to the\ntowns and villages. This bill would allow Steuben County to distribute\nnet collections as appropriate.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
